Write a self-contained Python 3 command-line script (intended to run under
Termux on Android, so use the shebang `#!/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/env
python`) that cleans the output of `pip freeze` in place, leaving only the
package names.
Requirements: **Purpose:** Read a single text file produced by `pip freeze` and
overwrite it so that it contains only one package name per line, with duplicates
removed and original order preserved. **Interface:** - Use `argparse` with a
description along the lines of "Clean pip freeze output and keep only package
names (overwrite file)." - Accept one required positional argument: the path to
the pip freeze output file. - Use `from __future__ import annotations` for
type-hint compatibility. **Input handling:** - Convert the argument to a
`pathlib.Path`.
If the path is not an existing regular file, exit with a system exit
(SystemExit) carrying an error message.
Ensure the error message variable is properly defined before use so the program
does not raise a NameError. - Read the file as UTF-8 with `errors="ignore"` and
split it into lines. **Name extraction (per line), function
`extract_package_name(line: str) -> str | None`:** 1.
Strip surrounding whitespace. 2.
Return None for empty lines and lines beginning with `#`. 3.
Return None for lines starting with `git+`, `http://`, or `https://` (VCS and
URL requirements are skipped). 4.
If the line contains `@` (direct references like `name @ url`), take the text
before the first `@`, strip it, and return it, or None if empty. 5.
Otherwise, match a precompiled verbose regular expression (compiled at module
level with `re.VERBOSE`) that: anchors at start, optionally allows a leading
`-e` followed by whitespace, then captures a named group `name` made of letters,
digits, underscores, dots, and hyphens.
Return the captured name, or None if there is no match. **Processing:** - Apply
extraction to every line, collect non-empty results in order. - Deduplicate
while preserving first-occurrence order (use a set for tracking seen names, in a
concise idiom). **Output:** - Overwrite the same file with the cleaned names
joined by newlines, with a single trailing newline, encoded as UTF-8. - Write
nothing else; no console output on success. **Entry point:** - Put the logic in
a `main()` function returning None, and invoke it under `if __name__ ==
"__main__":` with `raise SystemExit(...)` wrapping the call so the process exits
cleanly.
The exit call must be valid and must not reference an undefined name. **Style:**
Use type hints, keep code concise and idiomatic, and include brief comments only
where helpful. ---
